# rmscgate_backup.yaml.bak - an editor backup left in the services directory.
#
# EXERCISES  the same rejection path through the EXTENSION rather than the case:
#            the name must END in .yaml or .yml, so a trailing .bak fails the
#            regex. Kept beside rmscgate_Ignored because the two failures are
#            reported the same way but reached differently, and because this one
#            is what actually happens on a real machine - somebody edits a
#            definition in place and leaves the backup behind.
# UPSTREAM   not loaded; warned about, on stderr. Contrast rmscgate_rpmnew.yaml.rpmnew
#            in the base pack, which is the ONE non-matching name that is ignored
#            SILENTLY - the two together pin that the silent exception is narrow.
# RMSC       not loaded; stream expected to differ as above.
# BASIS      measured (the regex, and the rpmnew exception being the only silent
#            one).
# STAGING    none.
# ISOLATION  YES, with the rest of this case.
# FAILS IF   it loads, or it is ignored silently - the silent path is reserved
#            for rpmnew, and widening it would hide genuinely misnamed
#            definitions, which is exactly how a service goes missing with
#            nobody told.
name: RMSC gate backup file
start_cmd: /QOpenSys/usr/bin/true
check_alive: rmscgatedeadbak
